// Integrates `in` over time: `out` is `yStart` plus `k` times the
// integral of `in` since the first execute.  When `inReset` turns true,
// `out` is set to `inResetVal`, or to `yStart` when `inResetVal` is
// null.  This is the CDL `Reals.IntegratorWithReset` block.
//
// Unlike CDL, each step is the trapezoid from the last `in` to the current
// one, so `out` has direct feedthrough from `in`.  A stall, a step longer
// than both 1min and 10 times the longest of the last 8 steps, counts as
// the larger of the two.  Time while `in` is null, invalid or a fault is
// not integrated, and a reset while `inResetVal` is invalid or not finite
// waits until it is usable.  A null `in` sets `out` to null, an invalid
// `in` holds `out` with its status, and a fault holds `out` with fault,
// never null: a `k` or `yStart` that is not finite, an `in` that is not
// finite, or a step that overflows.  `out` has no unit.  The state is not
// persisted: after a restart `out` starts again from `yStart`.
Integrator: HxComp {
  // Input to integrate
  in: StatusNumber? <summary, transient>

  // Resets `out` when it turns true.  Optional.
  inReset: StatusBool? <summary, transient>

  // The value a reset sets `out` to.  When null a reset sets `yStart`.
  inResetVal: StatusNumber? <summary, transient>

  // Integrator gain
  k: Number 1

  // The value of `out` at the first execute
  yStart: Number 0

  // `yStart` plus `k` times the integral of `in`
  out: StatusNumber? <summary, transient, readonly, output>
}

// Approximates `k` times the derivative of `in`, filtered with time
// constant `T`: the transfer function `k * s / (T * s + 1)`, stepped by
// backward Euler, which is stable for any `T` and cycle.  This is the
// CDL `Reals.Derivative` block.
//
// Unlike CDL, `k` and `timeConst` (CDL's `T`) are slots, not inputs:
// link a `StatusNumberToNumber` to schedule them.  A stall, a step
// longer than both 1min and the larger of `timeConst` and 10 times the
// longest of the last 8 steps, is a gap, and so is time while `in` is
// null, invalid or a fault: `out` holds and the next step starts from
// there.  A null `in` sets `out` to null, an invalid `in` holds `out`
// with its status, and a fault holds `out` with fault, never null: a
// `timeConst` below 0, not finite or with a unit that is not a time, a
// `k` or `yStart` that is not finite, an `in` that is not finite, or a
// step that overflows.  `out` has no unit.
Derivative: HxComp {
  // Input to differentiate
  in: StatusNumber? <summary, transient>

  // Gain
  k: Number 1

  // Time constant `T` of the filter, in seconds unless it has a time unit
  timeConst: Number 1

  // The value of `out` at the first execute
  yStart: Number 0

  // Filtered derivative of `in`
  out: StatusNumber? <summary, transient, readonly, output>
}

// Limits the rate at which `out` follows `in`.  `out` approaches `in`
// at the rate `(in - out) / timeConst`, held between `fallingSlewRate`
// and `raisingSlewRate`.  While `enable` is false `out` is `in`.  This
// is the CDL `Reals.LimitSlewRate` block, and the CDL `Reals.Ramp` block
// with `active` linked to `enable` through a `StatusBoolToBool` and
// `timeConst` set to `raisingSlewRate` times 0.001 seconds.
//
// Unlike CDL, each step is a backward Euler step to the current `in`,
// so `out` has direct feedthrough from `in`.  A stall, a step longer
// than both 1min and 10 times the longest of the last 8 steps, counts
// as the larger of the two.  A null `in` sets `out` to null, an invalid
// `in` holds `out` with its status, and a fault holds `out` with fault,
// never null: a `raisingSlewRate` not above 0, a `fallingSlewRate` not
// below 0, either rate not finite or with a unit that does not fit
// `in`, a `timeConst` not above 0, an `in` that is not finite, or a
// step that overflows.  `out` has the unit of `in`.
SlewRateLimit: HxComp {
  // Input to follow
  in: StatusNumber? <summary, transient>

  // Fastest increase of `out`, in units of `in` per second, or in the
  // unit of `in` per the time unit it carries.  It must be above 0.
  raisingSlewRate: Number

  // Fastest decrease of `out`, in the units of `raisingSlewRate`.  It
  // must be below 0.  When null it is minus `raisingSlewRate`.
  fallingSlewRate: Number?

  // Time constant of the approach to `in`, above 0.  When null it is
  // `raisingSlewRate`, per second, times 10 seconds, the CDL default.
  timeConst: Duration?

  // When false `out` is `in`
  enable: Bool "true"

  // `in`, rate limited
  out: StatusNumber? <summary, transient, readonly, output>
}

// The average of `in` over the last `window` of time, with `in` taken
// as a straight line between executes.  Until a full window has passed,
// the average is over the time since the first execute plus 1E-10
// seconds, as ASHRAE 231 section 7.5.24 gives, so the first execute
// writes 0.  MBL (the Modelica Buildings Library) adds 1E-3 seconds, so
// the first seconds differ slightly.  This is the CDL
// `Reals.MovingAverage` block, with `window` for its `delta`.
//
// Time while `in` is null, invalid or a fault is left out of the
// average, and so is a stall, a step longer than both 1min and the
// larger of `window` and 10 times the longest of the last 8 steps.
// When a full window has no valid time `out` is `in`.  The component
// keeps one entry per execute in the window.  A null `in` sets `out` to
// null, an invalid `in` holds `out` with its status, and a fault holds
// `out` with fault, never null: a `window` below 10 microseconds, an
// `in` that is not finite, or a step that overflows.  `out` has the
// unit of `in`.
MovingAverage: HxComp {
  // Input to average
  in: StatusNumber? <summary, transient>

  // Length of time to average over, at least 10 microseconds
  window: Duration 1min

  // Average of `in` over the window
  out: StatusNumber? <summary, transient, readonly, output>
}
